Adreno speed-ups for dxvk-mobile (after dxvk_mobile_nocentroid.patch): a framebuffer cache (DXVK 1.9 made a VkFramebuffer,
a kernel allocation on the Qualcomm driver, at every render-target change; DXVK_FB_CACHE=0 turns it off), the window's
buffers at the game's size so the display scales them (DXVK_HWC_SIZE, set by the port when FSR is off), fragment-only
barriers between passes (DXVK_FRAG_BARRIERS), no blending on formats that cannot blend, and analysis switches
(DXVK_FRAMELOG, DXVK_PASSTIME, DXVK_PASSSEQ, DXVK_SKIP_STRETCH). Apply with patch -p1 inside private/deps/dxvk-mobile.

